ables the user to make linear ablations of varied lengths; and EPi-Sense Systems, a single-use disposable device used for the treatment of symptomatic, drug-refractory, and long-standing persistent atrial fibrillation. It also provides cryoSPHERE probe, which provides temporary pain relief by applying cryothermic energy to targeted intercoastal peripheral nerves in the ribcage; AtriClip System, an implantable device coupled to a single-use disposable applier; cryoXT probes, a cryoablation device designed specifically for Cryo Nerve Block therapy; LARIAT System, a solution for soft-tissue closure; Lumitip dissectors to separate tissues to provide access to key anatomical structures that are targeted for ablation; Glidepath guides for placement of clamps; and Subtle Cannula's to support access for EPi-Sense catheters. In addition, the company sells various reusable cardiac surgery instruments. It markets and sells its products through independent distributors and direct sales personnel. The company was incorporated in 2000 and is headquartered in Mason, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael H. Carrel | CEO, President & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $2.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $396K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 16%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $36K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $33K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["AtriCure, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $2.9B market cap on $535M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +17% over the past three years and +15% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -7% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 73% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $48M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -1.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 3.7% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 773% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":7.734440034647683},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 10.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $4.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (36% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Among the least levered in Healthcare \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Financial quality scores above most Healthcare peers","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"AtriCure (ATRC) Raised Guidance After A Profit Return, Is The Stock Cheap?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nasdaq-atrc/atricure/news/atricure-atrc-raised-guidance-after-a-profit-return-is-the-s","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794532729.768,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.956,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Did Profitable Quarter Just Shift AtriCure (ATRC) Stock Investment Narrative?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nasdaq-atrc/atricure/news/did-profitable-quarter-just-shift-atricure-atrc-stock-invest","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794444390.827,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.912,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"11,400 Shares in AtriCure, Inc. $ATRC Bought by Oregon Public Employees Retirement Fund","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/11400-shares-in-atricure-inc-atrc-bought-by-oregon-public-employees-retirement-fund.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794391897.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.919,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Understanding Momentum Shifts in (ATRC)","source":"news.stocktr